    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 Section 14",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990#sec-14"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "The matching agency carries out income matching of persons by\nusing any identification number for the purposes of personal\nassistance of a person to match:\n\n(a) income data of the person given to it by assistance agencies;\nand\n\n(b) except where the matching agency has, under paragraph 11,\ngiven particulars of a discrepancy in data about the person to\na source agency, the tax income data of the person given to\nthe matching agency in earlier steps;\nto find out if there are any inconsistencies in the income data of the\nperson.",
      "skos:definition": "The matching agency carries out income matching of persons by\nusing any identification number for the purposes of personal\nassistance of a person to match:\n\n(a) income data of the person given to it by assistance agencies;\nand\n\n(b) except where the matching agency has, under paragraph 11,\ngiven particulars of a discrepancy in data about the person to\na source agency, the tax income data of the person given to\nthe matching agency in earlier steps;\nto find out if there are any inconsistencies in the income data of the\nperson.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "00779ab59b51d6ec077ab79796e9154f7e6a34a0426c81804e35da718d95a6db",
      "skos:note": "The matching agency must carry out income matching of persons."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990#sec-14",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 Section 14",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "The matching agency carries out income matching of persons by\nusing any identification number for the purposes of personal\nassistance of a person to match:\n\n(a) income data of the person given to it by assistance agencies;\nand\n\n(b) except where the matching agency has, under paragraph 11,\ngiven particulars of a discrepancy in data about the person to\na source agency, the tax income data of the person given to\nthe matching agency in earlier steps;\nto find out if there are any inconsistencies in the income data of the\nperson."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to perform action",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14A Section 14A",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990#sec-14a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "If the source agency and the matching agency have agreed that this\nparagraph applies, the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(a) if the matching agency thinks that any results of a payment or\nincome matching appear to be results to which paragraph 15\napplies, the matching agency gives a sample to the source\nagency;\n\n(b) the source agency tests the sample;\n\n(c) if the source agency thinks the sample may be wrong, and\nthat the error may be corrected by adjusting an algorithm\nused by the matching agency, the source agency suggests the\nadjustment;\n\n(d) the matching agency makes the adjustment and repeats the\nrelevant parts of the matching;\n\n\nData-matching  Part 2\n\nSection 8\n\nData-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990\n\nCompilation date: 01/07/2026\n\n(e) subject to section 9, these subparagraphs apply as often as\nnecessary until the matching is complete;\n\n(f) if the source agency is an assistance agency, information\nexchanged under this paragraph may include the return of\nTFN data from the matching agency to the source agency;\n\n(g) the source agency must destroy the sample as soon as\npracticable after the matching is complete.\nSTEP 6",
      "skos:definition": "If the source agency and the matching agency have agreed that this\nparagraph applies, the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(a) if the matching agency thinks that any results of a payment or\nincome matching appear to be results to which paragraph 15\napplies, the matching agency gives a sample to the source\nagency;\n\n(b) the source agency tests the sample;\n\n(c) if the source agency thinks the sample may be wrong, and\nthat the error may be corrected by adjusting an algorithm\nused by the matching agency, the source agency suggests the\nadjustment;\n\n(d) the matching agency makes the adjustment and repeats the\nrelevant parts of the matching;\n\n\nData-matching  Part 2\n\nSection 8\n\nData-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990\n\nCompilation date: 01/07/2026\n\n(e) subject to section 9, these subparagraphs apply as often as\nnecessary until the matching is complete;\n\n(f) if the source agency is an assistance agency, information\nexchanged under this paragraph may include the return of\nTFN data from the matching agency to the source agency;\n\n(g) the source agency must destroy the sample as soon as\npracticable after the matching is complete.\nSTEP 6",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a0f47b5de3faa2ae01b9778672e643119ef7702e5ed5569854a75a0db80a31a5",
      "skos:note": "Source agency must test sample and suggest adjustment if necessary."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990#sec-14a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14A Section 14A",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "If the source agency and the matching agency have agreed that this\nparagraph applies, the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(a) if the matching agency thinks that any results of a payment or\nincome matching appear to be results to which paragraph 15\napplies, the matching agency gives a sample to the source\nagency;\n\n(b) the source agency tests the sample;\n\n(c) if the source agency thinks the sample may be wrong, and\nthat the error may be corrected by adjusting an algorithm\nused by the matching agency, the source agency suggests the\nadjustment;\n\n(d) the matching agency makes the adjustment and repeats the\nrelevant parts of the matching;\n\n\nData-matching  Part 2\n\nSection 8\n\nData-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990\n\nCompilation date: 01/07/2026\n\n(e) subject to section 9, these subparagraphs apply as often as\nnecessary until the matching is complete;\n\n(f) if the source agency is an assistance agency, information\nexchanged under this paragraph may include the return of\nTFN data from the matching agency to the source agency;\n\n(g) the source agency must destroy the sample as soon as\npracticable after the matching is complete.\nSTEP 6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-14a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
