      },
      "dc:source": "data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subject to subsection (5), where, solely or partly because of\ninformation given in Step 1, 4 or 6 of a data matching cycle, the tax\nagency considers taking action to issue an assessment or an\namended assessment of tax to a person, the agency:\n\n(a) must not take that action unless it has given the person\nwritten notice:\n\n(i) giving particulars of the information and the proposed\naction; and\n\n(ii) stating that the person has 28 days from the giving of\nthe notice in which to show cause in writing why the\naction should not be taken; and\n\n(b) must not take that action until the person has responded in\nwriting to the notice or the 28 days end, whichever occurs\nfirst.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Subject to subsection (5), where, solely or partly because of\ninformation given in Step 1, 4 or 6 of a data matching cycle, the tax\nagency considers taking action to issue an assessment or an\namended assessment of tax to a person, the agency:\n\n(a) must not take that action unless it has given the person\nwritten notice:\n\n(i) giving particulars of the information and the proposed\naction; and\n\n(ii) stating that the person has 28 days from the giving of\nthe notice in which to show cause in writing why the\naction should not be taken; and\n\n(b) must not take that action until the person has responded in\nwriting to the notice or the 28 days end, whichever occurs\nfirst.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-11-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-11-2-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-11-2-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f8bc554e315622060aa6e32bb1f49cbfbe5e9e820756becd46b549b9b024afcf",
      "skos:note": "Tax agency must give written notice and wait for response before taking action.",
      "dc:description": "written notice and response"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990#sec-11-2-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11(2) Notice of proposed action",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subject to subsection (5), where, solely or partly because of\ninformation given in Step 1, 4 or 6 of a data matching cycle, the tax\nagency considers taking action to issue an assessment or an\namended assessment of tax to a person, the agency:\n\n(a) must not take that action unless it has given the person\nwritten notice:\n\n(i) giving particulars of the information and the proposed\naction; and\n\n(ii) stating that the person has 28 days from the giving of\nthe notice in which to show cause in writing why the\naction should not be taken; and\n\n(b) must not take that action until the person has responded in\nwriting to the notice or the 28 days end, whichever occurs\nfirst."
    },
