    {
      "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-12-2-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12(5) Rules relating to privacy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990#sec-12-2-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(5) After the 3-year period ending on 30 June 1998, and after each\nsuccessive 3-year period, each agency must give the Minister\nresponsible for the agency a report for presentation to the\nParliament including all the details relating to the data-matching\nprogram carried out during the period that are specified for the\npurposes of this subsection in rules issued under this section.\nNote:\nSection 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 sets time limits for\ngiving reports to Ministers and for presentation of reports to the\nParliament.\n\n\nData-matching  Part 2\n\nSection 13\n\nData-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990\n\nCompilation date: 01/07/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(5) After the 3-year period ending on 30 June 1998, and after each\nsuccessive 3-year period, each agency must give the Minister\nresponsible for the agency a report for presentation to the\nParliament including all the details relating to the data-matching\nprogram carried out during the period that are specified for the\npurposes of this subsection in rules issued under this section.\nNote:\nSection 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 sets time limits for\ngiving reports to Ministers and for presentation of reports to the\nParliament.\n\n\nData-matching  Part 2\n\nSection 13\n\nData-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990\n\nCompilation date: 01/07/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-12-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-12-2-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-12-2-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ce2e69a6156481439fecabc5ddaacf87f963ee0e854f3c45fa07efa2d1fb7967",
      "skos:note": "Agency must provide report to Minister on data-matching program",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990#sec-12-2-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12(5) Rules relating to privacy",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(5) After the 3-year period ending on 30 June 1998, and after each\nsuccessive 3-year period, each agency must give the Minister\nresponsible for the agency a report for presentation to the\nParliament including all the details relating to the data-matching\nprogram carried out during the period that are specified for the\npurposes of this subsection in rules issued under this section.\nNote:\nSection 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 sets time limits for\ngiving reports to Ministers and for presentation of reports to the\nParliament.\n\n\nData-matching  Part 2\n\nSection 13\n\nData-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990\n\nCompilation date: 01/07/2026"
    },
